**user**:
> How do I remove the numbers on the axes and the box around a figure in ggplot?
**assistant**:
> In `ggplot2`, you can remove the numbers on the axes (axis text) and the box around the figure (also known as the plot border) by customizing the plot theme. Here's how you can do it:
> 
> ```r
> library(ggplot2)
> 
> # Create a basic ggplot
> p <- ggplot(mtcars, aes(x = wt, y = mpg)) +
>   geom_point()
> 
> # Modify the theme to remove axis text and the plot border
> p + theme(
>   axis.text = element_blank(),      # Remove axis numbers
>   panel.border = element_blank(),   # Remove the box around the plot
>   axis.ticks = element_blank(),     # Optionally, remove axis ticks as well
>   panel.background = element_blank() # Make the background transparent
> )
> ```
> 
> This setup uses `element_blank()` to effectively remove these elements from the plot. You can adjust which specific components are blanked out depending on your styling preferences. If you want to keep certain features while removing others, you'll need to specify each element individually.
